            "comment": "KidsFirst; The MP term definition for chordee MP:0003555 specifies acute angulation of the penis upon erection and places chordee under abnormal penile erection MP:0001379, unlike HPO which places Chordee HP:0000041 under Abnormal penis morphology HP:0000036 and provides details on the direction of bowing and degree of angulation. I think the match is therefore close and the MP term should be placed under both abnormal penile erection and morphology (see https://educalingo.com/en/dic-en/chordee)",
